/* book exam traps: Octane number is a volume percentage of iso-octane in a reference blend, not a percentage of iso-octane in the petrol itself. | MON is lower than RON for the same fuel because the motor test is harsher; sensitivity is RON − MON, not MON − RON. | The 10 % point governs cold starting and vapour lock, the 90 % point governs oil dilution and deposits. Swapping them is a common slip. | A lower calorific value per kg does not mean less energy per cylinder: what counts is the energy per kg of mixture. | Use the standard deviation, not the range, in COVimep, and divide by the mean IMEP, not by the peak pressure. */
